{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BraidsAndKnots.FrobeniusAntipodeLeanStub","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BraidsAndKnots.FrobeniusAntipodeLeanStub","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chirality_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chirality_real","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/frobenius-antipode-lean-stub.lean#L187-L194","doc":"The chirality factor is real and bounded: on the scalar model it\nis identically `1` (the trivial chirality of an unbraided word). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chirality_multiplicative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chirality_multiplicative","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/frobenius-antipode-lean-stub.lean#L172-L185","doc":"The chirality factor is multiplicative over independent\npn crossings (per construction).  On the scalar model every\nfactor is the trivial `1`, so the product of two independent\nfactors equals the factor of either — recorded here as the\nconcrete `1 · 1 = 1` instance of multiplicativity.  The general\nper-pn-crossing product lives in the basis-vector model. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chiralityFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chiralityFactor","kind":"def","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/frobenius-antipode-lean-stub.lean#L155-L170","doc":"**Chirality factor via antipode (Term 5).**\n\nFor a braid word β ∈ B_n with image T_w ∈ H_n(q), the chirality\nfactor is the per-pn-crossing product of (1 + sign·h):\n\n  a_K(β) = ∏_{c ∈ pn-crossings} (1 + sign(c)·h).\n\nEquivalently:\n  a_K = product over pn-crossings of\n    (1 + (τ_sym(σ) - τ_sym(S(σ))))\n\nRef: prop:chirality-dual-space-derivation.\nConcrete model: returns 1 (the trivial chirality factor of an\nunbraided word). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:frobenius-self-pairing-chirality","label":"def:frobenius-self-pairing-chirality","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-self-pairing-chirality.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.symmetrize_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.symmetrize_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/frobenius-antipode-lean-stub.lean#L146-L153","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.antipodeSymmetrize","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.antipodeSymmetrize","kind":"def","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/frobenius-antipode-lean-stub.lean#L133-L144","doc":"**Symmetrized element under antipode.**\n\nFor x ∈ H_n(q), the Frobenius-symmetrized form\n  x_sym := (x + S(x))/2\nis invariant under S (involutive symmetrization).\n\nUsed in the neutron tower closure\n(prop:frobenius-antipode-unifies-chirality-and-tower). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markov_trace_antipode_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markov_trace_antipode_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/frobenius-antipode-lean-stub.lean#L114-L131","doc":"**Markov trace is S-invariant.**\n\nFor elements in the symmetric channel of $H_n(q)$,\ntr_M(S(x)) = tr_M(x).  More generally, tr_M ∘ S has a\nsign-twist depending on the parity of the braid word\n(Yekutieli's rigid dualizing complex).\n\nRef: [kassel1995], [yekutieli2010].\n\nWas an `axiom`; it is `rfl` on this file's scalar-coefficient model,\nwhere `antipodeS = id`.  Note that the sign-twist described above\ncannot appear in this type at all: with `antipodeS = id` the two\nsides are the same term, so no parity is being tracked.  The twisted\nstatement is the substantive one and is not formalised here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.antipode_involution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.antipode_involution","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/frobenius-antipode-lean-stub.lean#L101-L112","doc":"**Antipode is an involution: S² = id.**\n\nWas an `axiom`; it is `rfl` on this file's scalar-coefficient model,\nwhere `antipodeS = id` (as `antipode_on_generator` above already\nrelies on).  So the axiom asserted nothing beyond that model choice.\n\nRead it as a property of the model, not as the Hopf-algebraic\ninvolution: on the basis-vector Hecke model of\n`knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean`, where `S(σ_i) = σ_i - h·1`, `S² = id`\nis a real statement and is not proved here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.antipode_on_generator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.antipode_on_generator","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/frobenius-antipode-lean-stub.lean#L86-L99","doc":"**S(σ_i) = σ_i⁻¹**, where σ_i⁻¹ = σ_i - h·1 with h = q - q⁻¹.\n\nOn the scalar-coefficient model `antipodeS = id`, so the antipode\nfixes the Markov-trace coefficient of every generator.  The full\nstatement (`S(σ_i)` equals the basis vector `σ_i - h·1`) requires\nthe basis-vector Hecke model in `knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean`;\nhere we record the trace-coefficient invariance that the scalar\nmodel supports — `S(σ_i)` and `σ_i` have the same Markov trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.antipode_anti_hom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.antipode_anti_hom","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/frobenius-antipode-lean-stub.lean#L64-L84","doc":"**S is an anti-homomorphism.**\n\nS(a · b) = S(b) · S(a).\n\nRef: [kassel1995] Quantum Groups, Ch. III.\n\nWas an `axiom`; provable on this file's scalar-coefficient model,\nwhere `antipodeS = id` and `heckeMul` is real multiplication of\ntrace coefficients -- hence commutative, so the anti-homomorphism\nidentity collapses to `mul_comm`.\n\nAs with `antipode_involution` below, read it as a property of the\nmodel.  Anti-multiplicativity has content only where the algebra is\nnon-commutative and `S` is not the identity; on the basis-vector\nHecke model of `knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean` it is a real\nstatement that is not proved here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.heckeSigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.heckeSigma","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/frobenius-antipode-lean-stub.lean#L59-L62","doc":"Hecke generator σ_i.  Trace coefficient `0` in the scalar model\n(full Hecke generators live in the basis-vector model). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.heckeOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.heckeOne","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/frobenius-antipode-lean-stub.lean#L56-L57","doc":"Hecke-algebra unit (identity element).  Trace coefficient `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.heckeMul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.heckeMul","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/frobenius-antipode-lean-stub.lean#L50-L54","doc":"Hecke-algebra multiplication.  On the scalar-coefficient model,\nmultiplication is real multiplication of the trace coefficients. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovTrace","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/frobenius-antipode-lean-stub.lean#L46-L48","doc":"The Markov trace tr_M: H_n(q) → ℝ.  Returns the element's\n`coeff` (single-coefficient scalar model). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.antipodeS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.antipodeS","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/frobenius-antipode-lean-stub.lean#L40-L44","doc":"The Frobenius antipode S: H_n(q) → H_n(q).  On the scalar-\ncoefficient model the antipode is the identity (the trace\ncoefficient is preserved). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAlgebra.coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAlgebra.coeff","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/frobenius-antipode-lean-stub.lean#L38-L38","doc":"Coefficient of the element under the Markov pairing —\n`markovTrace` returns this directly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAlgebra.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAlgebra.mk","kind":"ctor","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/frobenius-antipode-lean-stub.lean#L35-L35","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAlgebra","kind":"structure","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/frobenius-antipode-lean-stub.lean#L31-L38","doc":"Abstract Hecke-algebra carrier.  Concrete model: a single\nreal scalar tracking the Markov-trace coefficient of the\nelement.  Concrete construction (full basis-vector form) lives\nin `QOU.HeckeH3` and `knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}